@* Rendered once by _HomeLayout, so it sits on the landing page, the shop and a product
   page alike, and not on the dashboard (which uses the other layout). Icon only: the
   green bubble is the one thing on this site everybody already recognises, and a caption
   beside it would only add noise. The name lives in aria-label for screen readers and in
   title for the mouse.
   A page can set ViewData["WhatsAppMessage"] before this renders to open a more specific
   conversation — the product page asks about that bottle instead of in general. *@
@{
    var message = ViewData["WhatsAppMessage"] as string;
}
<a class="wa-float"
   href="@ContactInfo.WhatsApp(message)"
   target="_blank"
   rel="noopener noreferrer"
   aria-label="Écrire à OliveMorocco sur WhatsApp"
   title="Écrire à OliveMorocco sur WhatsApp">
    <partial name="Icons/WhatsApp" />
</a>